# Optional. Leave this unset for local development: the app then calls the same-origin "/api" path and the Vite
# dev/preview server proxies it to the backend (http://127.0.0.1:8000, override with VITE_PROXY_TARGET). That works
# for localhost and LAN hosts, over http (npm run dev) and https (npm run dev:https).
# Set it only to point at a backend on another origin, and use https:// there when the page is https. In dev, an
# http:// value on an https page is ignored (with a console warning) and "/api" is used instead.
# VITE_API_URL=https://api.example.com/api
